Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:13:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(art): attach the derived locale's English rung at the
 asset funnel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported: Temple of Mystery and Time Wipe showed no card art under the
Simplified-Chinese art setting, despite live English images.

Two distinct defects.

1. The rung was attached in `useCardImage`, which reaches it only on its three
   override paths — tokens, a pinned source printing, an art chain. The ordinary
   path (`fetchCardImageAsset` / `…ByOracleId`, i.e. a card with no art
   preferences at all) builds its asset in `scryfall.ts` and never passed
   through that helper. With no second ladder step, that printing's Chinese
   image 404'd straight past the English art and rendered the text placeholder.
   The rung is now attached in `resolveImageAsset`, the one funnel every
   stored-image asset is built through.

2. The first attempt at (1) derived the rung from the asset's `src`, which
   `resolveImageUrl` had already localized — and `derivedArtSource` returns null
   for any host but `cards.scryfall.io`, so it silently produced `undefined`
   again. The rung is the English art of the SAME printing, so it must be
   derived from the pre-localization URL.

Both are pinned by a regression test over a real stored entry; the cards named
above are the reported cases (live Scryfall image, no Simplified-Chinese one).
